WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:03.080
What does it mean to have a pre-disease?"

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:06.480
If you have slightly elevated blood pressure,

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:09.600
does that mean that you're pre-stroke?

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.550
Or maybe in a sense, we're all pre-death?

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:20.620
In 2001, the American Diabetes Association

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.260
began to call a slightly elevated blood sugar

00:00:23.269 --> 00:00:25.169
level “prediabetes.”

00:00:25.169 --> 00:00:29.620
By 2005, the Centers for Disease Control adopted

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:32.940
ADA standards, and 41 million people were

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:35.160
estimated to be prediabetic,

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:39.699
in comparison to 21 million diabetics in the U.S.

00:00:39.699 --> 00:00:42.520
In 2010, The ADA broadened its definition

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:46.780
of the glycemic level that would constitute prediabetes.

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:49.660
When adopted by the CDC, tens of millions

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:52.510
more people were swept into the definition.

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:58.040
Today, 84 million American, 1 in 3 adults,

00:00:58.040 --> 00:00:59.890
are considered prediabetic.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:03.180
Meanwhile, the number of diabetics in the

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:07.770
country is significantly lower- 30 million people.

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:09.900
The majority of people who are at the lower

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:13.600
range of what the ADA calls pre-diabetes never

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:14.619
progress to diabetes.

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:17.680
This has been shown in many studies.

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:20.820
Prediabetes causes no symptoms or complications,

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:25.619
and some international organizations disavow the label.

00:01:25.619 --> 00:01:29.060
One of the problems that organizations like

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:31.520
the World Health Organization have with the

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:34.840
way in which pre-diabetes is defined and managed

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:38.539
in the United States and elsewhere is that,

00:01:38.539 --> 00:01:42.360
the subtext of all of these prevention programs

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:45.869
are that, people are essentially fat and lazy,

00:01:45.869 --> 00:01:48.480
and if they could only be more responsible,

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:51.300
eat better, exercise more, they could solve

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:53.060
their problem.

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:55.420
All of the programs are based on individual

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:59.820
clinical solutions to what is really a broad

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:02.420
socially-driven, economically-driven, problem

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:04.060
in our society.

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:07.100
One study done several decades ago

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:09.680
looked at people who were in low income housing,

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:12.940
and broke them into three groups: a control,

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:15.240
that received nothing, another group that

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:17.120
recieved a little assistance in finding new

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:19.960
housing, and a third that got vouchers and

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:23.360
assistance to relocate to better housing.

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:25.760
After 20 years, the people who got the most

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:29.160
help had the least diabetes and obesity, despite

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:34.420
not receiving nutrition and exercise counseling
or drugs.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:40.100
No one in this debate disputes that healthful

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:44.580
lifestyles, exercise, eating well, eating

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:47.040
the right foods, is vitally important for

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:49.830
everyone, but it stands to reason that more

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:53.380
money going into the socio-economic aspects

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:56.100
of the problem, could also be important in

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:57.480
solving the problem.

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:02.670
Funding is readily available to research pharmacological
solutions.

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:05.720
The incentives to build drugs that are targeted

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:08.180
to pre-diabetes are great.

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:12.840
And so far, the Food and Drug Administration has never

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:17.200
approved any drug specifically to treat pre-diabetes,

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:20.040
so the drug makers are a little bit hamstrung.

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:23.980
But there are drugs used for diabetes or obesity

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:26.940
that are prescribed to patients “off-label”

00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:28.780
for prediabetes.

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:30.720
Although some side effects from these drugs

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:34.460
are relatively benign, others can be life-threatening.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:39.300
These side effects are so serious that many

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:40.937
people have asked the question,

00:03:40.937 --> 00:03:44.060
“Does it make sense to even think about using these

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:46.980
drugs that could have life threatening consequences

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:50.440
to treat something that is a pre-disease?”

00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:55.520
In 2014, the ADA estimated that $44 billion dollars

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:57.880
were spent on pre-diabetic care.

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:00.760
This is where it starts to get sticky, the

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:04.220
profit motive, the motivations for using drugs,

00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:07.740
it enters a murky area where some of the people

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:11.780
making the advice also have financial conflicts

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:15.040
with the people who would profit from that

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:17.320
trend towards the use of drugs.

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:22.240
This so-called disease has spawned a gigantic

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:27.120
industry of everything from glucose testing

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:31.140
monitors, to herbal remedies that are hawked

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:34.540
online to naive patients.

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:39.600
Since the definition of pre-diabetes was made

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:44.460
and adopted by the CDC, the prevention budget

00:04:44.479 --> 00:04:48.800
that they have has risen dramatically.

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:51.720
It's clear that this has shifted the priorities

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:54.840
of the agency towards diabetes prevention

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:57.340
While some profit from the designation of

00:04:57.340 --> 00:04:59.840
prediabetes, patients are left to grapple

00:04:59.849 --> 00:05:03.060
with the consequences of an ambiguous diagnosis,

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:06.280
such as higher health care costs and lesser

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:07.940
health insurance options.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:10.520
It creates a lot of anxiety in people who

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:12.780
have been diagnosed with pre-diabetes.

00:05:12.780 --> 00:05:17.600
And especially, people who have limited abilities

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:21.060
to respond to that diagnosis in an effective

00:05:21.069 --> 00:05:23.900
way, because of their genetics, or because

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:26.780
of their social environment that they live in.

00:05:26.780 --> 00:05:29.580
If you have pre-diabetes designation, particularly

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:32.080
if you're prescribed a drug for it, then that's

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:34.100
a red flag for life insurers, and you may get

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:37.319
an unfavorable insurance rate.

00:05:37.319 --> 00:05:40.600
So, these are concrete ways that people's

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:44.060
lives could be diminished, and this is not

00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:46.180
to say, "You should never test people's blood

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:47.840
sugar," or "you should never alert people

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:50.000
to the importance of diet and exercise.”

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:53.440
The question is whether you should institutionalize

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:58.189
this very broad range, including a very mild

00:05:58.189 --> 00:06:02.940
elevation of blood sugar, as this terrible

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:06.360
problem of, "walking towards the cliff" and

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:10.340
"runaway train" that could harm people in these

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:14.600
disastrous ways, and that have institutional effects

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:17.640
downstream that cost money to solve

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:21.360
and create anxiety for patients.

